# A qualified data cardinality: owl:onDataRange. Before 0.2.0 it faulted the
# whole document (exit 3, no report). It is a data restriction, so it is an
# omission, labelled DataExactCardinality; the rest of the document is still
# classified. INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B .
:dp a owl:DatatypeProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :dp ;
                     owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; owl:onDataRange xsd:string ] .
